@extends('layouts/settings')
@section('body')

<!--
  Every pane in the window, rendered once and shown one at a time.

  Panes rather than routes: this window is 715px wide and never navigates —
  System Settings does not either. `settings-window.ts` matches a sidebar row's
  `data-pane-link` to a pane's `data-pane`, keeps a history so the back and
  forward arrows in the toolbar mean something, and remembers the last pane so
  reopening Settings lands where it was left.

  The markup describes; the wiring lives in `resources/scripts/settings-window.ts`.
  That is the split the rest of this app uses for anything that talks to the
  native side, and this window talks to it for the login item, the appearance
  the window itself resolves against, and its own version.
-->

<section class='set-pane' data-pane='general' data-pane-title='General'>
  <div class='set-card'>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Open at login</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>Adds SystemCleaner to your login items.</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-switch' type='button' role='switch' aria-checked='false'
              aria-label='Open at login' data-switch='openAtLogin'>
        <span class='set-knob' aria-hidden='true'></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Check for updates automatically</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>Once a day, in the background. Nothing installs on its own.</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-switch' type='button' role='switch' aria-checked='false'
              aria-label='Check for updates automatically' data-switch='autoCheckUpdates'>
        <span class='set-knob' aria-hidden='true'></span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class='set-section-title'>Reset</div>
  <div class='set-card'>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Restore default settings</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>Puts every switch on this window back where it started. Nothing on your disks is touched.</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-btn' type='button' data-action='resetPrefs'>Reset</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class='set-pane' data-pane='appearance' data-pane-title='Appearance'>
  <div class='set-card'>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Theme</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>Both windows, and the material behind them.</span>
      </span>
      <div class='set-segmented' role='radiogroup' aria-label='Theme'>
        <button class='set-segment' type='button' role='radio' aria-checked='false'
                data-option='colorMode' data-value='light'>Light</button>
        <button class='set-segment' type='button' role='radio' aria-checked='false'
                data-option='colorMode' data-value='dark'>Dark</button>
        <button class='set-segment' type='button' role='radio' aria-checked='false'
                data-option='colorMode' data-value='system'>Auto</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class='set-card-note'>
    Auto follows the Mac, including a sunset switch. Light and Dark pin the app
    and tell the window to resolve its material the same way, so the page and
    the window buttons never disagree.
  </p>
</section>

<section class='set-pane' data-pane='notifications' data-pane-title='Notifications'>
  <div class='set-card'>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>When a long scan finishes</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>Only when SystemCleaner is not the window in front.</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-switch' type='button' role='switch' aria-checked='false'
              aria-label='Notify when a long scan finishes' data-switch='notifyOnFinish'>
        <span class='set-knob' aria-hidden='true'></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>When scheduled cleaning runs</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>What it reclaimed, after the fact.</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-switch' type='button' role='switch' aria-checked='false'
              aria-label='Notify when scheduled cleaning runs' data-switch='notifyOnSchedule'>
        <span class='set-knob' aria-hidden='true'></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>When an update is available</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>For SystemCleaner itself, not for the rest of the Mac.</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-switch' type='button' role='switch' aria-checked='false'
              aria-label='Notify when an update is available' data-switch='notifyOnUpdate'>
        <span class='set-knob' aria-hidden='true'></span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class='set-card-note'>
    macOS decides whether a notification is shown at all. If none arrive, look
    for SystemCleaner in System Settings › Notifications.
  </p>
</section>

<section class='set-pane' data-pane='cleaning' data-pane-title='Cleaning'>
  <div class='set-card'>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Confirm before deleting</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>Ask once more before anything leaves the disk.</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-switch' type='button' role='switch' aria-checked='false'
              aria-label='Confirm before deleting' data-switch='confirmDeletes'>
        <span class='set-knob' aria-hidden='true'></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Reveal what a clean removed</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>Writes each run to the cleanup history the Quick Clean screen reads.</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-switch' type='button' role='switch' aria-checked='false'
              aria-label='Reveal what a clean removed' data-switch='recordHistory'>
        <span class='set-knob' aria-hidden='true'></span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class='set-section-title'>Never Touched</div>
  <div class='set-card'>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Protected paths</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>Folders no clean is allowed to enter.</span>
      </span>
      <span class='set-card-value' data-value='protectedCount'>&mdash;</span>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Kept cookies</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>Sites that stay signed in when browser data is cleaned.</span>
      </span>
      <span class='set-card-value' data-value='keptCookieCount'>&mdash;</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class='set-card-note'>
    Both lists are edited where the things in them are: the Privacy screen in
    the main window.
  </p>
</section>

<section class='set-pane' data-pane='schedule' data-pane-title='Schedule'>
  <div class='set-card'>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Scheduled cleaning</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>Runs Quick Clean on its own, over the targets the Schedule screen picked.</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-switch' type='button' role='switch' aria-checked='false'
              aria-label='Scheduled cleaning' data-switch='scheduleEnabled'>
        <span class='set-knob' aria-hidden='true'></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'><span class='set-card-label'>How often</span></span>
      <select class='set-select' data-select='scheduleFrequency' aria-label='How often'>
        <option value='daily'>Daily</option>
        <option value='weekly'>Weekly</option>
        <option value='monthly'>Monthly</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Include browser data</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>Caches and histories, minus anything on the keep-list.</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-switch' type='button' role='switch' aria-checked='false'
              aria-label='Include browser data' data-switch='scheduleIncludePrivacy'>
        <span class='set-knob' aria-hidden='true'></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Empty the Trash afterwards</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>A scheduled clean moves what it can to the Trash; this is what finishes the job.</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-switch' type='button' role='switch' aria-checked='false'
              aria-label='Empty the Trash afterwards' data-switch='scheduleEmptyTrash'>
        <span class='set-knob' aria-hidden='true'></span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class='set-card'>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>When it runs</span>
      </span>
      <span class='set-card-value' data-value='scheduleDescription'>&mdash;</span>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Last run</span>
      </span>
      <span class='set-card-value' data-value='scheduleLastRun'>Never</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class='set-card-note'>
    The time of day, and which folders it cleans, are set on the Schedule
    screen in the main window.
  </p>
</section>

<section class='set-pane' data-pane='privacy' data-pane-title='Privacy'>
  <div class='set-card'>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Everything stays on this Mac</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>Scans, results and cleanup history are written to this machine and never sent anywhere.</span>
      </span>
      <span class='set-card-value'>
        <span class='i-f7-lock-shield-fill' style='width: 16px; height: 16px; color: var(--green);' aria-hidden='true'></span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Share anonymous usage data</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>There is nothing to share. SystemCleaner collects no analytics.</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-switch' type='button' role='switch' aria-checked='false'
              aria-label='Share anonymous usage data' data-switch='analytics' disabled>
        <span class='set-knob' aria-hidden='true'></span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class='set-section-title'>Access</div>
  <div class='set-card'>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Full Disk Access</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>Without it, caches in protected folders are invisible to every scan.</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-btn' type='button' data-action='openFullDiskAccess'>Open</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class='set-card-note'>
    Opens System Settings › Privacy &amp; Security. macOS does not let an app
    grant itself access, so the switch there is the only one that counts.
  </p>
</section>

<!--
  Software Update.

  The same shape System Settings gives it, and the same data the Updates screen
  in the main window already reads: `updatesXData()` is that screen's state,
  loaded here unchanged. What differs is the arrangement — the app's own update
  is the card at the top, and everything else on the Mac is a row under "Also
  Available", which is where a person looks for it.
-->
<section class='set-pane' data-pane='software-update' data-pane-title='Software Update'>
  <script src='/updates-xdata.js'></script>
  <div x-data='updatesXData()'>
    <div class='set-card'>
      <div class='set-card-row' style='align-items: flex-start; padding-top: 14px;'>
        <span class='set-tile' data-tone='blue' aria-hidden='true'
              style='width: 38px; height: 38px; border-radius: 9px;'>
          <span class='i-f7-arrow-down-circle-fill' style='width: 22px; height: 22px;'></span>
        </span>
        <span class='set-card-row-text' style='gap: 3px;'>
          <span class='set-card-label' style='font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.01em;'
                x-text='selfHeadline()'>SystemCleaner</span>
          <span class='set-card-hint' x-show='selfDetailLine()' x-cloak x-text='selfDetailLine()'></span>
        </span>
        <button class='set-btn' type='button' @click='checkSelfUpdate()'
                :disabled="self.stage === 'checking' || self.stage === 'downloading' || self.stage === 'installing'">
          Check Now
        </button>
        <button class='set-btn set-btn-primary' type='button' x-show="self.stage === 'available'" x-cloak
                @click='downloadSelfUpdate()'>
          Download
        </button>
        <button class='set-btn set-btn-primary' type='button' x-show="self.stage === 'ready'" x-cloak
                @click='installSelfUpdate()'>
          Restart to Install
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class='set-card-row' x-show="self.stage === 'downloading'" x-cloak>
        <span class='set-card-row-text'>
          <span class='set-card-hint' x-text='selfProgressLabel()'></span>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class='set-card-row' x-show='self.releaseNotes' x-cloak>
        <span class='set-card-row-text'>
          <span class='set-card-hint' style='white-space: pre-wrap;' x-text='self.releaseNotes'></span>
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class='set-section-title'>Also Available</div>
    <div class='set-card'>
      <div class='set-card-row'>
        <span class='set-card-row-text'>
          <span class='set-card-label'>macOS</span>
          <span class='set-card-hint' x-text="systemOutdatedCount() > 0 ? systemOutdatedCount() + ' update available' : 'Up to date'"></span>
        </span>
        <button class='set-btn' type='button' data-action='openSoftwareUpdate'>Open</button>
      </div>
      <div class='set-card-row'>
        <span class='set-card-row-text'>
          <span class='set-card-label'>Homebrew</span>
          <span class='set-card-hint' x-text="brewTotal() + ' outdated'"></span>
        </span>
        <span class='set-card-value' x-text="brewFormulae.length + ' formulae · ' + brewCasks.length + ' casks'"></span>
      </div>
      <div class='set-card-row'>
        <span class='set-card-row-text'>
          <span class='set-card-label'>Pantry</span>
          <span class='set-card-hint' x-text="pantryOutdated.length + ' outdated'"></span>
        </span>
        <span class='set-card-value' x-text="pantryTrackedCount + ' tracked'"></span>
      </div>
      <div class='set-card-row'>
        <span class='set-card-row-text'>
          <span class='set-card-label'>Applications</span>
          <span class='set-card-hint' x-text="desktopOutdated.length + ' outdated'"></span>
        </span>
        <span class='set-card-value' x-text="desktopApps.length + ' scanned'"></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class='set-section-title'>This Mac</div>
    <div class='set-card'>
      <div class='set-card-row'>
        <span class='set-card-row-text'><span class='set-card-label'>Installed</span></span>
        <span class='set-card-value' x-text="macosVersion ? 'macOS ' + installedLabel() : '—'"></span>
      </div>
      <div class='set-card-row'>
        <span class='set-card-row-text'><span class='set-card-label'>Command Line Tools</span></span>
        <span class='set-card-value' x-text="clToolsInfo.version || 'Not installed'"></span>
      </div>
      <div class='set-card-row'>
        <span class='set-card-row-text'>
          <span class='set-card-label'>Last checked</span>
        </span>
        <span class='set-card-value' x-text='lastCheckedLabel()'>—</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class='set-card-foot'>
      Updating SystemCleaner quits it and relaunches the new copy. Everything
      else here is a count of what the rest of your Mac has waiting; the
      Updates screen in the main window is where you act on it.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class='set-pane' data-pane='storage' data-pane-title='Storage'>
  <div class='set-card'>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>Startup disk</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint' data-value='diskUsage'>&mdash;</span>
      </span>
      <span class='set-card-value' data-value='diskAvail'>&mdash;</span>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'>
        <span class='set-card-label'>SystemCleaner's own data</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint'>~/Library/Application Support/SystemCleaner</span>
      </span>
      <button class='set-btn' type='button' data-action='revealDataDir'>Show</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class='set-card-note'>
    What is taking up the rest of it, and the scans that work it out, are on
    the Disk Usage screen in the main window.
  </p>
</section>

<section class='set-pane' data-pane='about' data-pane-title='About'>
  <div class='set-card'>
    <div class='set-card-row' style='padding-top: 16px; padding-bottom: 16px;'>
      <span class='set-tile' data-tone='blue' aria-hidden='true'
            style='width: 44px; height: 44px; border-radius: 10px;'>
        <span class='i-f7-sparkles' style='width: 24px; height: 24px;'></span>
      </span>
      <span class='set-card-row-text' style='gap: 3px;'>
        <span class='set-card-label' style='font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.015em;'>SystemCleaner</span>
        <span class='set-card-hint' data-value='appVersion'>—</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'><span class='set-card-label'>Computer</span></span>
      <span class='set-card-value' data-value='hostName'>—</span>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'><span class='set-card-label'>macOS</span></span>
      <span class='set-card-value' data-value='osVersion'>—</span>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'><span class='set-card-label'>Chip</span></span>
      <span class='set-card-value' data-value='cpuModel'>—</span>
    </div>
    <div class='set-card-row'>
      <span class='set-card-row-text'><span class='set-card-label'>Memory</span></span>
      <span class='set-card-value' data-value='memory'>—</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class='set-card-foot'>
    SystemCleaner is a local tool. It reads this Mac, writes to this Mac, and
    talks to nothing else.
  </p>
</section>

@endsection
